  "item.naraka.god_blood": "§lGod Blood",
  "item.naraka.god_blood.tooltip.0": "Used as a crafting material for powerful equipment.",
  "item.naraka.god_blood.tooltip.1": "It can also be charged into a 'Soul Stabilizer' to forge powerful gear.",
  "item.naraka.god_blood.tooltip.2": "The essence behind a name shrouded in fear and awe is a gluttony to fill a void.",
  "item.naraka.god_blood.tooltip.3": "Unable to gain color, yearning for color, it sought to strip away colors and add them to itself.",
  "item.naraka.god_blood.tooltip.4": "Yet no matter what is added, black remains black. Even its remaining ashes are merely pitch-black emptiness.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_phase_1_disc": "Herobrine Phase 1 Disc",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_phase_2_disc": "Herobrine Phase 2 Disc",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_phase_3_disc": "Herobrine Phase 3 Disc",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_phase_4_disc": "Herobrine Phase 4 Disc",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_scarf": "Herobrine Scarf",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_scarf.tooltip.0": "Can be worn in the chestplate slot, or combined with armor using a 'Soul Smithing Block'.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_scarf.tooltip.1": "Along the inner lining of the cape, the image of 'Naraka' where it once existed flickers.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_scarf.tooltip.2": "However, this merely reflects it; one cannot enter or leave 'Naraka' through this.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_spawn_egg": "Herobrine Spawn Egg",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_totem": "Herobrine Totem",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_totem.tooltip.0": "Can summon Herobrine by stacking 2 Blocks of Imitation Gold, a Herobrine Totem, and 1 Netherrack from bottom to top, then setting it on fire.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_totem.tooltip.1": "Herobrine can only be summoned within a 'Herobrine Sanctuary' structure.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_totem.tooltip.2": "A monument engraved with its face.",
  "item.naraka.herobrine_totem.tooltip.3": "When the false gold catches its eyes and guides its footsteps, this vessel summons and binds its physical body to this world.",
  "item.naraka.imitation_gold_block": "Block of Imitation Gold",
  "item.naraka.imitation_gold_block.tooltip.0": "When placed, it turns adjacent Iron Blocks into Blocks of Imitation Gold.",
  "item.naraka.imitation_gold_block.tooltip.1": "Also used to duplicate 'Herobrine Totems'.",
  "item.naraka.imitation_gold_block.tooltip.2": "Gold holds brilliance, and brilliance summons it.",
  "item.naraka.imitation_gold_block.tooltip.3": "This gold is a false creation, holding a fainter brilliance than genuine gold.",
  "item.naraka.imitation_gold_block.tooltip.4": "Yet precisely because it is a false brilliance, it is all the more effective in guiding its steps.",
  "item.naraka.locked_health": "Locked Health",
  "item.naraka.mighty_holy_spear": "Mighty Holy Spear",
  "item.naraka.mighty_holy_spear.tooltip.0": "Bless the mineral swords infused with eight distinct souls, and use them together as materials to craft the ultimate weapon.",
  "item.naraka.mighty_holy_spear.tooltip.1": "The Tyrant has fallen, yet the 'Naraka' still demands one to reign.",
  "item.naraka.mighty_holy_spear.tooltip.2": "Regicide, prove thy worthiness to claim the throne through eight trials of tribulation.",
  "item.naraka.naraka_fireball_staff": "Naraka Fireball Staff",
  "item.naraka.naraka_pickaxe": "Scythe of Ruin",
  "item.naraka.naraka_pickaxe.tooltip.0": "Can be used as a pickaxe or an axe.",
  "item.naraka.naraka_pickaxe.tooltip.1": "Wandering through otherworldly realms in search of 'Color', it trampled and absorbed everything in its path.",
  "item.naraka.naraka_pickaxe.tooltip.2": "An entity that always appears through Naraka, leaving only void in the worlds it invades before vanishing.",
  "item.naraka.naraka_pickaxe.tooltip.3": "Thus, in some worlds it is called the 'God of Void', and in others, the 'Tyrant of Naraka'.",
  "item.naraka.nectarium": "Nectarium",
  "item.naraka.nectarium.tooltip.0": "Edible. Consuming it fully restores Saturation, Hunger, and Health.",
  "item.naraka.nectarium.tooltip.1": "In a certain alternate dimension, it is said that those who break their contracts shall suffer the 'Wrath of the Rock'.",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_block": "Block of Nectarium",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_core": "Nectarium Core",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_core.tooltip.0": "Can be activated using a Honey Bottle, generating Nectarium Crystals upon activation.",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_core.tooltip.1": "Plants, ores... they're both just things you 'extract' from the earth, right?",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_core.tooltip.2": "Therefore, this is a revolutionary crop designed to save 22nd-century humanity.",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_crystal": "Nectarium Crystal",
  "item.naraka.nectarium_ore": "Nectarium Ore",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.blessed.tooltip.0": "Armor that yields supreme power through the resonance of mutual gluttony.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.blessed.tooltip.1": "Two souls—yet one—touching without satisfaction, devour each other and wail in endless agony.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.soul.tooltip.0": "Wearing all 4 pieces of Purified Soul Armor forged from the same mineral and holding a sword forged from that same mineral activates the 'Challenger' buff.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.soul.tooltip.1": "Defeating Herobrine with the 'Challenger' buff active bestows a blessing upon the sword and destroys all equipped armor.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.soul.tooltip.2": "The challenger must wear the soul stabilized through satisfied craving, wield it as a weapon, and lay back to rest the entity that failed to shed its yearning.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.soul.tooltip.3": "By doing so, its soul will resonate with the stabilized soul to find peace, and its blessing shall be bestowed upon the weapon held by the challenger.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.tooltip.0": "Can be forged at a Soul Smithing Block using minerals or God Blood.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.tooltip.1": "The purest vessel.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.tooltip.2": "To use it in a ritual, it must first be attuned using soul-infused minerals.",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_armors.tooltip.3": "Or, by using its blood—",
  "item.naraka.purified_soul_boots": "Purified Soul Boots",
